# 20. ACCESSIBILITY AND INCLUSIVE UX

Make the application comfortable and usable for a broad audience.

Requirements:

- Keyboard navigation.
- Visible focus states.
- Screen-reader labels.
- Sufficient text contrast.
- Clear button names.
- Reduced-motion support.
- Scalable text.
- Touch-friendly targets.
- Accessible modal behavior.
- Escape-key dismissal where appropriate.
- Alternative controls for essential pet interactions.
- Non-color indicators for status.
- Pause controls for optional animations and sound.

Provide a simplified visual mode if 3D performance is poor.

Essential reminder management must remain possible even when the 3D scene fails to load.

The pet should not be the only way to access important functionality.

