At 10:30 AM, a reminder is delivered through an available notification channel.

Milo performs a gentle attention animation if the application is active and the user has enabled it.

A message appears:

"Hey, Alex! Let's grab some water together."

Alex drinks water and marks the reminder complete.

The reminder is recorded as completed.

Alex earns a treat.

Milo wags his tail.

Alex selects Feed.

Milo receives the treat and performs a happy animation.

The treat inventory decreases correctly.

The bond progress updates.

### Day 1: Task completion

At 11:00 AM, Alex receives a task reminder.

Alex opens the checklist and completes the required items.

The checklist updates correctly.

Alex completes the parent reminder.

The application records the completion and grants the configured reward once.

Milo celebrates.

### Day 1: End of day

Alex completes the wrap-up reminder.

Milo settles beside his bed.

The room transitions into its evening atmosphere.

Alex sees a summary of completed reminders and can prepare tomorrow's routine.

### Day 2: Return

Alex opens PAWSE again.

The pet profile and room state load from persistent storage.

Milo recognizes Alex's saved preferred name.

Milo performs a greeting animation.

The application does not replay the onboarding flow.

Previously completed reminders remain in the history.

New reminders are shown according to their schedule.

### Later: Growth milestone

After the configured growth requirements are met, Milo reaches a new stage.

The application triggers a short celebration.

A new animation or accessory becomes available.

The milestone appears in the pet journal.

The room and existing reminders remain intact.

This journey must work from beginning to end without manual database edits or page refreshes to trigger expected behavior.

